# RELAY settings — copy this file to ".env" (same folder), paste your key, save,
# then restart Relay. Everything here is optional: with nothing filled in, RELAY still
# works fully offline (its own voice, its own speech recognition, all its commands).
# Never commit .env: it holds your keys. (.gitignore already excludes it.)

# ---- AI answers through FreeLLMAPI (or any OpenAI-compatible /v1 router) ----
# This is all you need for ChatGPT-style spoken answers.
# FreeLLMAPI desktop app on this PC: http://127.0.0.1:31415/v1 (Docker / source: 3001).
# The key is on the Keys page of its dashboard.
# For other people's PCs, host the router somewhere they can reach (https://...).
RELAY_LLM_URL=
RELAY_LLM_KEY=

# ---- OPTIONAL: Sarvam, one key for everything. Leave empty for the offline voice ----
# One key turns on BOTH the Bulbul voice (what RELAY says) and Saaras speech recognition
# (what you say; Indian accents, Hindi/Tamil/... understood as English commands).
# Key from https://dashboard.sarvam.ai -> API keys.
SARVAM_API_KEY=
# More Sarvam settings: remove the # at the start of a line to use it.
# A Bulbul voice name, e.g. shubh (empty = Sarvam's default voice):
# SARVAM_SPEAKER=
# SARVAM_TTS_MODEL=bulbul:v3
# Accent of the voice (RELAY talks in English):
# SARVAM_LANGUAGE=en-IN
# off = keep only the voice; your speech is recognised offline on this PC instead
# (with Saaras on, the wake word is still checked on this PC before anything is sent):
# SARVAM_STT=off
# Your own gateway that adds the real key, for public builds:
# SARVAM_BASE_URL=https://your-gateway.example.com/sarvam
